  "diagnosis": [
    "English MIRACL has higher snapshot coverage and higher unconditional Hit@10, MRR@10 and nDCG@10 than Chinese MIRACL.",
    "Chinese compatibility cases score higher than English compatibility cases, but the small language subsets are not paired equivalents and cannot isolate language quality.",
    "Both compatibility runs return results for most or all expected-missing probes, so abstention is not calibrated.",
    "English descriptive and cross-language compatibility queries are the clearest ranking failures; group sizes are small and are used only to set the next benchmark target.",
    "Latency is host- and corpus-size-dependent; the bilingual table records it for operations, not as a language-quality comparison."
  ],
